{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md .pose/rules/backend-go.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; cat .pose/results/delivery-validation.json | head -c 3500; rg -n 'gitCommandContext|not a git repository|runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmittedContext|TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator' pose-mcp/internal/pose; rg -n 'Git|locale|review|validation' POSE.md | head -35; rg -n 'git|locale' .pose/knowledge --glob '*.md' | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-15\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates: spec:pose-check-shares-the-federated-material@defect-fix\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:governance-git-reads-untranslated\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer o motor ler o stderr dos comandos Git de governança sem tradução, de modo que um diretório fora de qualquer repositório seja reconhecido como tal em qualquer locale.\n\n### Business value\nA checagem de paridade do espelho do Harness, que o harne8 roda também numa sessão `pt_BR.UTF-8`, reprovou com o pose-dist em `26b011d`: o teste `TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator`, da spec `pose-check-shares-the-federated-material`, acusou \"Git context could not be proved at the project root\". A descoberta de módulos classifica a falha de `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` procurando \"not a git repository\" no stderr, e em pt_BR o Git escreve a frase traduzida: um projeto fora de qualquer repositório ficava com o fechamento desconhecido. O motor já roda em `LC_ALL=C` os comandos cujo stderr ele lê fora da governança (`gitOutputUntranslated`, spec `pose-git-repository-detection-ignores-locale`); os comandos de governança não.\n\n### Constraints\n- Só o ambiente dos comandos Git de governança muda; a saída de plumbing que eles produzem não depende do locale.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Mudar os comandos Git fora da captura de governança.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: Every Git command the governance read view runs shall run with `LC_ALL=C` and `LANGUAGE=C`, so a failure classified by its stderr is classified the same way under any locale.\n\n### Non-functional\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Security\n- Nenhuma mudança.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Em `LC_ALL=C`, nada muda.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/governance_read_view_git.go`: o ambiente do executor dos comandos de governança.\n\n### Artifacts\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_git_untranslated_test.go\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:governance-git-reads-untranslated module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção por toda leitura de governança que roda Git (`pose check`, `pose index`, revisões). Check permanente `governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated|TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Nenhum: os comandos são de plumbing, e o ambiente de exec do Go usa o último valor de uma chave repetida.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] `LC_ALL=C` e `LANGUAGE=C` no executor de governança (R1).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Teste do coordenador rodado sob pt_BR, que reprova sem a mudança.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Context: a classificação lê o stderr em inglês.\n- Options considered: (a) reconhecer também a frase traduzida; (b) rodar os comandos de governança sem tradução.\n- Decision: (b).\n- Basis: R1\n- Rationale: (a) teria de conhecer cada tradução do Git; (b) é o mecanismo que o motor já adota para os outros comandos cujo stderr lê.\n- Consequences: todo stderr de Git que a governança classifica está em inglês.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nO teste do coordenador, sob `LC_ALL=pt_BR.UTF-8`, `LANGUAGE=pt_BR`; pulado onde o Git não está traduzido.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26, Git traduzido para pt_BR.\n- Notes: a paridade do espelho em pt_BR, rodada pelo harne8 com o pose-dist em 26b011d, reprovou só em `TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator`. Sem a mudança, `TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated` reprova com a mesma mensagem; com ela, passa.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: a governança classifica a falha do Git do mesmo jeito em pt_BR.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated check:governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\n\n### Known gaps\n- O teste é pulado numa máquina sem a tradução do Git para pt_BR.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-15T20:45:55Z\",\n  \"mode\": \"strict\",\n  \"git_head\": \"ea3d5d5246f2e5a6e4d8b90bb4724aaa3a7e68a8\",\n  \"matrix_sha256\": \"sha256:9c24d532cf2c618a5fe1d559df6c77409e379968c266bddbbc9c8a7adfa576ad\",\n  \"provenance_digest\": \"sha256:b618f3b826f358bc0673031c5f7a222a7826b046a3d808d1af51a5fc7511707b\",\n  \"scope_provenance\": {\n    \"artifact-claims-stop-at-the-section-end\": \"sha256:c0083ea34012c3ec78814d53d3bdb83918132e90f23fee8ff51903aee8672622\",\n    \"calendar-dates-tolerate-utc-stamping\": \"sha256:36f9125ec27177733affb1bfac1d5dddc2a61a6e2bddbabca5207aad9946e5d6\",\n    \"check-builds-the-delivery-graph-once\": \"sha256:3174d521faa7402018e6ae4d4997e54e202161c3ecce5b4b201fe562d4f9aa62\",\n    \"check-strict-verdict-n